Expose async shader compilation as a libretro core option

The Vulkan renderer can compile a shader it has never seen on worker threads
and skip the draws that need it until it is ready
(RasterizerVulkan::AccelerateDrawBatchInternal: wait_built is false when
Settings::values.async_shader_compilation is on, except for draws of six
vertices or fewer, which still wait). The Android and Qt frontends offer it; the
libretro core never sets it, so it stays at its default, off, and every new
shader stops the emulation thread until the GPU driver returns.

On an iPhone 14 Pro (Majora's Mask 3D, MoltenVK, 2026-10-19) the game held 60
fps at 5.7 to 6.4 ms of work per frame, and stopped for 1 to 4 seconds each
time a scene was drawn for the first time; the disk shader cache only helps
on the second visit.

This adds the option `citra_async_shader_compilation` (default disabled, so a
frontend that does not set it sees no change) and reads it with the other
graphics options.

